Publish ACPI SCMI clocks through an exact firmware-node provider lookup while
retaining ordinary DT provider behaviour. The CIX clock-table driver supplies
the provider identity, and the SCMI core serialises lookup against supplier
unbind before returning a clock-hardware reference.

Provenance: based on cixtech/cix-linux-main revision
bc078a383042a6c14b05c56e12390e422f893088. Provider identity, bounds and
lifetime validation, complete ACPI publication, and the CIX-scoped
unused-clock policy are overlay-maintained corrections regenerated for Linux
7.2.

